USER TABLE
==========

Purpose: Holds user records.

Proposed PostgreSQL fields
--------------------------
- Id: INTEGER identity primary key
- Display name: TEXT, required; duplicates allowed
- Email: TEXT, required and unique; managed by the authentication provider; private and not shown on the public profile
- Authentication provider user ID: TEXT, required and unique
- Password: Managed by the authentication provider; not stored in the app database
- DOB: DATE, required; stored for 20+ eligibility and kept private
- Age: Derived from DOB only to verify the user is 20+; not stored separately or shown to other users
- City: TEXT, required; shown on the user's profile
- State/province: TEXT, required; shown on the user's profile
- Interests: Optional Interest[] in the TypeScript app model; stored through UserInterest records, not as a User column

These PostgreSQL types are a working draft. Authentication-provider-specific details may change when the provider is selected.

Relationships
--------------
- A user can select multiple interests; the connections are stored through UserInterest records.
- A user can host multiple meetings; each meeting has one host.
- A user can request to attend multiple meetings; these connections are tracked through RSVP records.
- Hosted and RSVP'd meetings are retrieved when needed, not stored as lists on the User record.